WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.910
No matter how many Oscars they have in their
display case, every actor on the planet will

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.149
give a bad performance sooner or later.

00:00:07.149 --> 00:00:11.599
Perhaps a critically beloved actress will
pick up a lousy screenplay, or maybe a respected

00:00:11.599 --> 00:00:14.759
star is having a particularly bad day on set.

00:00:14.759 --> 00:00:19.160
Whatever the reason, even the best actors
have given truly awful performances that will

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.310
live forever in Hollywood infamy.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:24.279
Here, we're celebrating some of the worst.

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:26.439
Matthew McConaughey – The Dark Tower

00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:31.860
After years of embarrassing himself with box
office flops, Matthew McConaughey finally

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:37.250
broke free from his rom-com curse by sleazing
it up in Magic Mike, nailing Interstellar,

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.270
and winning Best Actor for Dallas Buyers Club.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:44.030
With all that under his belt, McConaughey
seemed like the perfect choice to play the

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.320
villain in The Dark Tower.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.640
"You are like a dog fetching a stick over
and over."

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:54.780
But sadly, the 2017 Stephen King adaptation
bombed with critics, flopped at the box office,

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.920
and earned McConaughey some pretty dark reviews.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.920
Slate's Sam Adams wrote,

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.550
"McConaughey's matter-of-fact evil […] reads
more like the indifference of a check-cashing

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:05.780
movie star."

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:10.300
And Michael O'Sullivan of The Washington Post
said the actor's performance was: "Unlikely

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:14.440
to evoke deathly shivers so much as a terminal
case of the giggles."

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:18.290
But Alison Willmore of Buzzfeed had the best
burn of all when she wrote,

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:22.920
"Matthew McConaughey offers up what's basically
a more evil version of whatever he's doing

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.480
in those Lincoln car commercials."

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.130
"1,800 pounds and do whatever the heck I want."

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:31.680
"I can respect that."

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.640
Cate Blanchett – Indiana Jones and the Kingdom
of the Crystal Skull

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:41.320
Screen legend Cate Blanchett won Best Actress
for Blue Jasmine, wowed critics with Carol,

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.909
and hammed it up to everyone's delight in
Thor: Ragnarok.

00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:47.980
But hey, nobody's perfect—something she
learned with Indiana Jones and the Kingdom

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:49.190
of the Crystal Skull.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.650
"I want to know.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:54.110
I want to know.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:55.340
Tell me.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.540
I'm ready.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.040
I want to know!"

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:04.050
Blanchett came off as silly and forgettable
in a part that Peter Travers described as:

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:08.560
"A one-note villain role with an accent that
conjures up Rocky and Bullwinkle more than

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.090
the desired red menace."

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:13.780
If any other actress had played the part,
we wouldn't care as much, but this is Cate

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:14.870
Blanchett.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:17.310
She's capable of so much more.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.640
Eddie Redmayne – Jupiter Ascending

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:24.950
In 2015 Eddie Redmayne won the Worst Supporting
Actor Razzie for his performance in Jupiter

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:29.690
Ascending — which ironically hit theaters
just a few days before Redmayne won his Best

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:31.440
Actor Oscar for The Theory of Everything.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.970
But while his performance as the disabled
physicist was flawless, we can't say the same

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:40.810
for his turn as the space titan, who wildly
modulates between murmuring and shouting.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:43.590
"I create life."

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.910
Stephanie Merry of The Washington Post wrote,

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:51.310
"Redmayne raises his voice to epic soprano
levels when reaming out his otherworldly lackeys.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.810
If he's capable of inflicting damage, it's
to eardrums alone."

00:02:54.810 --> 00:03:00.540
In an over-the-top movie, Redmayne sticks
out as the most outrageous thing in the film.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.709
Natalie Portman – Star Wars

00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:06.530
When Natalie Portman is on her game, she's
an absolute phenom.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.450
That's why she won Best Actress for Black
Swan.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:12.959
But of course, not every performance deserves
a little gold statue—witness the horrors

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.250
of the Star Wars prequel trilogy.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:19.349
"Anakin all I want is your love."

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:21.730
"Love won't save you, Padme."

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:26.640
Maybe it was the corny dialogue, or the zero
chemistry she had with her leading man.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.349
Whatever the reason, Portman was one of the
worst parts of the trilogy, which is really

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:31.910
saying something.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:34.319
Jake Gyllenhaal – Okja

00:03:34.319 --> 00:03:38.540
It's fair to say Jake Gyllenhaal is one of
the best actors in Hollywood today, starring

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:43.629
in fan favorites like Stronger, Donnie Darko,
and End of Watch...and that's what makes Okja

00:03:43.629 --> 00:03:45.099
so utterly baffling.

00:03:45.099 --> 00:03:50.530
This Korean sci-fi flick follows a little
girl trying to rescue an oversized swine from

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.860
the clutches of a meat-crazed corporation.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:56.280
And the most annoying character she runs across
is Gyllenhaal's.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:00.140
"Well f---ing film me, Jennifer.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:01.820
Can't fake these emotions."

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:07.740
Dana Stevens of Slate wrote, "There are performances
said to be 'as broad as a barn,' and then

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.410
there's Gyllenhaal's performance."

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.170
And Kyle Buchanan of Vulture said Gyllenhaal
was...

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:14.629
"So flamboyant, you can see it from space."

00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:18.909
Gyllenhaal responded to the criticism by saying
he loved the reactions and that his performance

00:04:18.909 --> 00:04:20.479
was meant to be polarizing.

00:04:20.479 --> 00:04:23.729
Well then that's the one thing he totally
nailed.

00:04:23.729 --> 00:04:25.830
Johnny Depp – Mortdecai

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:29.599
Alright — It's been a long time since anyone
called Johnny Depp a great actor.

00:04:29.599 --> 00:04:33.830
Sure, he won some praise for Black Mass, but
for the most part, he's been wearing silly

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:38.270
disguises, using ridiculous accents, and slumming
it in movies like Alice Through the Looking

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.270
Glass.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:44.559
But once upon a time, Depp was a living, breathing
masterclass in playing weirdos and screwballs.

00:04:44.559 --> 00:04:49.439
He even delivered solid performances in more
realistic films like Donnie Brasco and What's

00:04:49.439 --> 00:04:50.860
Eating Gilbert Grape?

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:55.710
Therefore, Mortdecai perfectly sums up what's
become of Depp's once-impressive career.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:05:00.199
"Have we taken a wrong turn and arrived on
the set of an adult film?"

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:05.540
It's a performance based solely on physical
tics, funny voices, and absolutely no substance.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:08.940
"Run I shall like a bloody gazelle.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.040
Mortdecai…

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:12.560
I've always been in tip top shape."

00:05:12.569 --> 00:05:16.029
As film critic Peter Sobczynski put it, Depp's
performance was…

00:05:16.029 --> 00:05:19.229
"On the level of a below-average knock-knock
joke."

00:05:19.229 --> 00:05:23.619
And the Razzies agreed, nominating him for
Worst Actor in 2016.

00:05:23.619 --> 00:05:28.339
Domestic audiences weren't impressed either,
as Mortdecai grossed just $7.6 million at

00:05:28.339 --> 00:05:29.339
home against a $60 million budget.

00:05:29.339 --> 00:05:30.339
"I'll make it up to you Jacques-y."

00:05:30.339 --> 00:05:35.499
"Oh, I know you will, sir, you always do."

00:05:35.499 --> 00:05:36.860
Thanks for watching!

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.400
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.529
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

